export anchor CasinoFeltStyle:
    number: 240
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Casino felt
    idea:
        The dashboard is laid out on a dark green felt table inside a padded
        leather rail, with the four figures as stacked chips, the projects
        dealt as a fanned hand of dark cards with corner indices, and the
        fortnight drawn as chip stacks.
    base: dark
    palette:
        rail: #1c120c, the page, the padded rail, the header and the style sheet
        leather: #26180f, the activity log, fields and the style sheet panels
        felt: #0f3d2c, the table surface at its edges
        feltLight: #145238, the lit centre of the table, the brightest felt any text sits on
        card: #0d2a1f, project cards and chip centres
        gold: #e2c376, the table line, card borders, the primary button, this week chips, links and focus
        goldInk: #1c120c, text on gold
        ivory: #f3eedd, text, figures and last week chip outlines
        sage: #c3cdb9, meta, labels and axis text
        chipRed: #a8323c, the edge of the active projects chip, decoration only
        chipBlue: #2f5d9a, the edge of the due this week chip, decoration only
        ok: #a8f0c0, On track text and check circle
        risk: #f6cf72, At risk text and triangle
        bad: #ffaba0, Behind and overdue text, crossed square, clock and the overdue chip edge
    type:
        Two stacks. Display text uses Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Georgia,
        serif, with the greeting 36px italic, section titles 26px, chip
        figures 28px bold and card corner indices 22px bold. Text uses
        Franklin Gothic Medium, Arial Narrow, Arial, sans-serif at 15px and
        1.5, card names 16px at 600, labels and meta 12px caps at 600 tracked
        0.12em.
    layout:
        A dark rail header holds a gold diamond mark with the Brightwork name,
        the six nav links as caps text with a gold underline on Home, a
        leather search field, a bell, a gold New project button and Mara
        Okafor. Below, the table is a felt panel with 56px rounded ends, a
        radial light in its centre, a 14px padded leather rail around it and a
        thin gold line inset 16px from the edge. On the felt the greeting is
        centred in italic display type with the date and a coral line reading
        4 tasks are overdue with a clock. The four figures are poker chips in
        a row, each a striped edge ring round a dark centre with the number,
        and a caps label below, overdue on a coral edged chip. The projects
        are dealt as a fanned hand of six dark cards with gold borders, each
        tilted a few degrees, with the percent and status symbol as the top
        left index and repeated upside down at bottom right, and the name,
        category, status word, tasks and due date in the middle over a thin
        gold meter. Below the table sit two panels on the rail, the chart as
        chip stacks for each weekday, last week as ivory outlined chips and
        this week as gold chips with counts on top, and the dealer's log of
        activity with gold rules. Below 1100px the hand stops fanning and
        becomes a three column grid, below 640px a two column grid, chips go
        two by two and the panels stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 40px table padding, 16px card padding, 24px between chips.
    density: Medium low. The table is roomy and the cards are small but few.
    corners: 56px rounded table ends, 10px cards, round chips, 6px buttons and fields.
    borders:
        A 14px leather rail, a 1px gold line inset in the felt, 1px gold card
        borders with a second inner gold line.
    shadows:
        Cards cast 0 10px 20px of black at 45 percent onto the felt, chips
        cast 0 4px 0 of a darker rim, and the felt has an inner vignette.
    icons:
        Line icons at 1.8px stroke. Status uses a check circle, a triangle
        with a bang and a crossed square, shown as the card index symbol and
        with the word, overdue a clock.
    focus: A 2px gold outline offset 3px.
    tone:
        Light and a little playful, such as The hand, Chips this week and
        Dealer's log, never gambling talk.
